* ''Plaintext on disk only'' (operator, 2026-11-19: //"I'm ok with these layers of wikis getting projected in the clear (the human can get eyes on that content more readily in early alpha)"//, then //"I only meant the plaintext on disk, you found a real bug then"//; lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/state/decisions #/open). The disk projection of a face's personal layers may rest in clear through early alpha, where the human's own eyes reach it. A personal slot document resting CLEAR in a hearth store (found in four: root, notes, lararium, works) counts as a security bug, never as the ruling's reach: Lares-Awakens' Personal-Ward (PR #315) seals every margin and draft the worn face names, and road (b) removes the island copies (ranks 18a and 34).

